# The built frontend is output, not source. `core.autocrlf` is true on this
# machine, so git kept the assets LF in the index and CRLF in the working
# tree -- and every `npm run build --workspace web-ui` then reported files
# vite had written byte-for-byte identically as modified. A 724 kB three.js
# chunk showed up in `git status` on every rebuild with nothing in it changed,
# which is exactly the noise that teaches a reader to skim past `git status`.
#
# Bytes as the bundler wrote them, no conversion either way.
src/poieo/web/static/** -text

# vite copies this template into the bundle byte for byte, so its line endings
# end up in checked-in output. Left to `core.autocrlf` it is CRLF on Windows and
# LF elsewhere, and the same commit then builds two different bundles -- which is
# how CI first found this. Pin it, and the build is reproducible across machines.
web-ui/index.html text eol=lf
